-- title:
--   Hilbert 90 for L⊗_K K_∞, cyclic case
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ and $L$ be number fields with $L$ an extension of $K$ that is Galois, and let $\sigma$ be a $K$-algebra automorphism of $L$ such that every $K$-algebra automorphism $\tau$ of $L$ lies in the subgroup of integer powers of $\sigma$ (so $\mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ is cyclic, generated by $\sigma$). Write $K_\infty$ for the infinite adele ring `InfiniteAdeleRing K`, and let $\sigma\otimes\mathrm{id}$ denote the ring endomorphism [`AutomorphicForm.sigmaTensor K L (InfiniteAdeleRing K) σ`](def/AutomorphicForm_TwistedOrbital.html#L199) of $L\otimes_K K_\infty$, which by definition is the underlying ring homomorphism of the algebra map $\sigma\otimes\mathrm{id}_{K_\infty}$ on the tensor product. The assertion is: for every $x\in L\otimes_K K_\infty$ such that the product over $i$ ranging through $0,1,\dots,n-1$, where $n=\operatorname{finrank}_K L$, of the $i$-th iterates $(\sigma\otimes\mathrm{id})^{i}(x)$ — taken in that order as the product of the list indexed by `List.range n` — equals $1$, there exists a unit $y$ of the ring $L\otimes_K K_\infty$ with $x=(\sigma\otimes\mathrm{id})(y)\cdot y^{-1}$.
--
--   This is Hilbert's Satz 90 in the form of vanishing of the first cohomology of the cyclic group $\mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ acting on the units of the Galois algebra $L\otimes_K K_\infty$, the archimedean component of the adelic setting. It is used in the treatment of twisted orbital integrals for automorphic forms, being cited by [`AutomorphicForm.eq_inv_mul_of_isTwistedWeightedOrbitalIntegralOn_of_normString_eq_toTensorGL_diagonal_of_coupled_one_smul_infiniteAdeleRing`](thm.html#AutomorphicForm.eq_inv_mul_of_isTwistedWeightedOrbitalIntegralOn_of_normString_eq_toTensorGL_diagonal_of_coupled_one_smul_infiniteAdeleRing) and [`AutomorphicForm.exists_units_eq_inv_mul_unitsMap_sigmaTensor_of_norm_eq_one`](thm.html#AutomorphicForm.exists_units_eq_inv_mul_unitsMap_sigmaTensor_of_norm_eq_one).
